something is kind then it chases the dog.** (Given).\n13. **If something needs the lion then it is round.** (Given).\n\nFrom the information, we know:.\n- The dog is round (from point 1).\n- The dog needs the tiger (from point 2).\n- The tiger is red (from point 5).\n- The mouse sees the tiger (from point 4).\n- Therefore, by point 6, the tiger is kind.\n\nNow, let\'s consider the statement "The mouse is not round":.\n- From point 10, if something chases the dog, it is round. Since the dog is round, chasing the dog would make it round.\n- From point 11, if something is round, it sees the lion. Since the dog is round, the dog sees the lion.\n- From point 12, if something is kind, it chases the dog. Since the dog is round, the dog chases the mouse (because the dog needs the tiger and the tiger is kind).\n- From point 13, if something needs the lion, it is round. Since the dog needs the tiger and the tiger is round, the dog is round.\n\nSince the dog is round and the dog chases the mouse, the mouse must be round to chase the dog. Therefore, the mouse cannot be not round.\n\nThus, the statement "The mouse is not round" is false.\n\n**Final Answer: B) False**.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
